WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.340
Rest in peace, the last of the Marvel-Netflix
superhero series.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:10.180
On Monday, February 18th, 2019, Deadline delivered
harrowing news to the masses - both The Punisher

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:13.200
and Jessica Jones have been cancelled at Netflix.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.380
The two streaming shows that stood strong
after Netflix pulled the plug on Luke Cage,

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:22.359
Iron Fist, and the much-loved Daredevil in
an unprecedented axe-swinging session in late

00:00:22.359 --> 00:00:27.109
2018, The Punisher and Jessica Jones helped
make up the Marvel Television corner of the

00:00:27.109 --> 00:00:28.970
streamer's content library.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:33.079
Their cancellations mean that there are no
longer any non-cancelled, Netflix-backed Marvel

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:34.530
shows on the platform.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:38.960
The Punisher's axing comes just a month after
the series aired its highly anticipated second

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.489
season to critical praise and fanfare from
loyal viewers.

00:00:42.489 --> 00:00:46.950
The standing plans are that Jessica Jones
season 3 will air sometime later this year,

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:51.210
giving the series a chance to wrap up its
story, which The Punisher sadly didn't get

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.210
to do.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:56.929
Around the time formal word got out, Punisher
star Jon Bernthal took to his Instagram account

00:00:56.929 --> 00:01:00.019
to address the show's cancellation, saying,
in part,

00:01:00.019 --> 00:01:01.410
"To all who have served.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.410
All who know loss.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.810
All who love and understand Frank and his
pain.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:06.690
It has been an honor to walk in his boots.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:10.940
I'm endlessly grateful to the comic fans and
the men and women of the Armed Services and

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.330
law enforcement community who Frank means
so much to."

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:18.620
Marvel Television head honcho Jeph Loeb penned
a letter to Marvel fans, thanking them for

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.170
supporting all the shows.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:21.180
He said, in part,

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.940
"Our Network partner may have decided they
no longer want to continue telling the tales

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:28.100
of these great characters… but you know
Marvel better than that.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.901
As Matthew Murdock's Dad once said, 'The measure
of a man is not how he gets knocked to the

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.850
mat, it's how he gets back up.'"

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.750
Loeb teased at the very end of his letter
that the stories may not completely be over

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:40.090
yet, writing "to be continued…!"

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:44.250
This double cancellation comes as Disney,
which owns Marvel Studios and its small-screen

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:49.950
arm Marvel TV, prepares to roll out its upcoming
direct-to-consumer streaming platform Disney+.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:54.640
The company has several projects brewing — including
multiple series centered on Marvel Cinematic

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:59.820
Universe heroes Vision and Scarlet Witch,
Loki, and Falcon and the Winter Soldier.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:04.360
Popular speculation is that Netflix is cutting
ties with the Marvel series so that Disney

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:09.509
can potentially scoop up the shows, revive
them, and air them on Disney+ alongside the

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:10.690
other Marvel shows.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:15.341
However, there are two factors complicating
this idea: First, according to Variety, there

00:02:15.341 --> 00:02:20.489
is reportedly a clause in the original agreement
between Marvel TV and Netflix for Luke Cage,

00:02:20.489 --> 00:02:25.849
Iron Fist, Daredevil, and Jessica Jones that
legally bars Marvel TV from using any of the

00:02:25.849 --> 00:02:32.030
series' characters in a non-Netflix show or
TV movie for at least two years post cancellation;

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:36.659
and second, according to Deadline, Loeb recently
entered a deal for four television series

00:02:36.659 --> 00:02:40.680
and a special with none other than Hulu, another
massive streamer.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:45.370
If what we know about the terms of Marvel
TV's deal with Netflix is correct, fans shouldn't

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:50.230
expect to see any of the Marvel-Netflix series
get resurrected — for Hulu, Disney+, or

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.209
any other platform — for at least two years.

00:02:53.209 --> 00:02:57.090
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Netflix,
quote, "did not have any ownership stake"

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:01.069
in its Marvel superhero shows, all of which
were owned by Disney.

00:03:01.069 --> 00:03:05.519
Netflix cancelling Jessica Jones and The Punisher
now, plus the three other solo shows last

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:09.849
year, signifies that Disney is hoping to reclaim
the series that it doesn't have direct possession

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:12.519
over — and those are the ones on Netflix.

00:03:12.519 --> 00:03:16.440
Sad as everyone may be over Netflix doing
away with The Punisher and Jessica Jones,

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:20.579
the two silver linings here are that Jessica
Jones will still release a third season, and

00:03:20.579 --> 00:03:24.719
that we certainly haven't seen the last of
Bernthal, who will appear in The Many Saints

00:03:24.719 --> 00:03:28.450
of Newark, New Line Cinema's in-development
prequel to The Sopranos.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:33.489
Additionally, all signs are pointing to Disney
as the future of Marvel TV fare, with executives

00:03:33.489 --> 00:03:38.209
at both Disney and Marvel having reportedly
stated that, quote, "the cancelled Netflix

00:03:38.209 --> 00:03:40.609
fare could live again on Disney+."

